
Vacuum circuit breakers are commonly used in medium-voltage power distribution systems where reliable switching and fault interruption are required.

Their main function is to open and close electrical circuits and interrupt current under specified operating and fault conditions.

When selecting a vacuum circuit breaker, engineers need to consider more than rated voltage.

Rated current, short-circuit breaking capacity, insulation level, operating mechanism, installation conditions, and system configuration all need to be evaluated.

The breaker also needs to work correctly with the associated switchgear and protection system.

Outdoor and indoor installations may have different environmental requirements, so the application conditions should be provided when requesting equipment.

